  "narrative": {
    "intro": "District of Columbia has $249M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The District recorded 1,146 awards with an average award size of $217K. Obligations fell 99.3% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show a sharp drop from prior full-year totals: FY26 recorded $33.2B, FY25 recorded $31.4B, FY24 recorded $36B, FY23 recorded $33.9B, and FY22 recorded $31.6B. Department-level spending in FY2027 to date is concentrated: the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $61.8M, the General Services Administration obligated $49.2M, and the Department of Transportation obligated $33.1M. Vendor-level flows are also focused: SALIENT CRGT, INC. received $19.5M, GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. received $19.3M, and GRUNLEY CONSTRUCTION CO., INC. received $17.2M. Industry obligations cluster in information and engineering work: Other Computer Related Services received $50.4M, Engineering Services received $38M, and Computer Systems Design Services received $23.1M. Current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date activity only.",
    "sections": [
